   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law, in relation to requiring state agencies\nthat issue requests for proposals to provide notification to elected officials\nfor requests for proposals for projects in excess of ten million dollars",
    "basePrintNo": "S2939",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2939-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 7,
       "fullName": "Anna Kaplan",
       "imgName": "1044_Anna_Kaplan.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1224,
       "sessionMemberId": 1817,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "KAPLAN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §136-d, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2939\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to requiring state\nagencies that issue requests for proposals to provide notification to\nelected officials for requests for proposals for projects in excess of\nten million dollars\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would requires state agencies and authorities that issue RFPs\nin excess of $10 Million Dollars to notify the elected officials who\nrepresent the affected zip codes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would requires state agencies and authorities that issue RFPs\nin excess of $10 Million Dollars to notify the elected officials who\nrepresent the affected zip codes.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCommunity participation in large developments is critical not only for\neconomic success but for the holistic empowerment of the neighborhood\nwherein the project lies. While many notification requirements exist in\nlaw, such as newspaper advertisements, no actual notification of elected\nofficials who represents the areas of a subject RFP is required by law-\nthis is a gross and unwise oversight, particularly in this day and age\nwhen notification can be delivered instantaneously by virtual means.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
